              "id": "glog-87d1249f-449d-453c-af34-99854d4d5264",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe `pyCrypto` library, along with its `pad` module, is deprecated and no longer actively maintained. This poses a security risk as deprecated libraries may contain unpatched vulnerabilities. It is recommended to use the `pyca/cryptography` library, which is actively maintained and provides a more secure and modern approach to cryptographic operations.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n- Replace the deprecated `pyCrypto` library with the `pyca/cryptography` library.\n- Regularly update your dependencies to ensure you are using the latest, most secure versions.\n- Review and refactor your code to use the new library's API.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the use of `pyCrypto`'s `pad` function with `pyca/cryptography`'s padding functionality. Here is an example of how you can modify your code:\n\n```python\n# Original code using pyCrypto\nfrom Crypto.Util.Padding import pad\n\ndata = b\"example data\"\nblock_size = 16\npadded_data = pad(data, block_size)\n\n# Updated code using pyca/cryptography\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import padding\n\ndata = b\"example data\"\nblock_size = 128  # block size in bits for cryptography library\npadder = padding.PKCS7(block_size).padder()\npadded_data = padder.update(data) + padder.finalize()\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nTo execute the updated code example, you need the following library:\n\n- `cryptography`\n\nYou can install it using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install cryptography\n```\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)"
