            {
              "id": "glog-ae12bbd2-0d0e-48d8-87ac-2eded051b88b",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe `pyCrypto` library, including its `unpad` module, is deprecated and unmaintained. This poses a security risk as deprecated libraries may contain vulnerabilities that are not patched. The recommended alternative is the `pyca/cryptography` library, which is actively maintained and provides a more secure and modern approach to cryptographic operations.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n- Replace the use of the `pyCrypto` library with the `pyca/cryptography` library.\n- Regularly update your dependencies to ensure you are using the latest, most secure versions.\n- Review and refactor your code to use secure cryptographic practices.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the deprecated `unpad` function from `pyCrypto` with the equivalent functionality from the `pyca/cryptography` library. Here is an example of how you can modify your code:\n\n```python\n# Original code using pyCrypto\nfrom Crypto.Util.Padding import unpad\n\n# Example usage\ndef decrypt_and_unpad(ciphertext, key, iv):\n    # Decrypt the ciphertext\n    plaintext_padded = decrypt(ciphertext, key, iv)\n    # Unpad the plaintext\n    plaintext = unpad(plaintext_padded, block_size)\n    return plaintext\n\n# Updated code using pyca/cryptography\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import padding\n\n# Example usage\ndef decrypt_and_unpad(ciphertext, key, iv):\n    # Decrypt the ciphertext\n    plaintext_padded = decrypt(ciphertext, key, iv)\n    # Unpad the plaintext\n    unpadder = padding.PKCS7(block_size * 8).unpadder()\n    plaintext = unpadder.update(plaintext_padded) + unpadder.finalize()\n    return plaintext\n```\n\n### Library Dependencies\n\nTo execute the updated code example, you need the following library:\n\n- `cryptography`\n\nYou can install it using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install cryptography\n```\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Cryptographic Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cryptographic_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-327: Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/327.html)"
